@startuml EndPointFirmaDigitalX509
title Endpoints y Flujo para Certificados y Firmas

actor "Admin Dept" as admin
actor "Usuario" as user
participant "certificate-service" as cert
participant "hsm-service" as hsm
participant "signing-service" as signing

== 1. GENERACIÓN DE CERTIFICADO (Admin) ==
admin -> cert: POST /api/v1/certificates/generate
cert -> hsm: POST /api/v1/keys/user-key-pair
hsm --> cert: { "key_id": "user1_priv" }
cert -> hsm: GET /api/v1/keys/{key_id}/public-key
hsm --> cert: public_key_pem
cert -> cert: Crear CSR con public_key + datos
cert -> hsm: POST /api/v1/keys/sign-csr
note right: Firma CSR con dep-key
hsm --> cert: CSR firmado → Certificado X.509
cert --> admin: { "key_id": "...", "certificate": "pem" }

== 2. FIRMA DE DOCUMENTO (Usuario) ==
user -> signing: POST /api/v1/sign
signing -> signing: Calcular hash SHA-256
signing -> cert: GET /api/v1/certificates/{key_id}
cert --> signing: Certificado X.509 (pem)
signing -> hsm: POST /api/v1/keys/sign
note right: Firma hash con user_private_key
hsm --> signing: Firma digital
signing -> signing: Construir paquete PKCS#7
signing --> user: Documento firmado

== 3. VERIFICACIÓN (Cualquiera) ==
user -> signing: POST /api/v1/verify
signing -> signing: Extraer firma y certificado
signing -> cert: POST /api/v1/certificates/validate
cert --> signing: Certificado válido
signing -> hsm: POST /api/v1/keys/verify
note right: Verifica firma con public_key del certificado
hsm --> signing: Resultado verificación
signing --> user: ✅ Firma válida / ❌ Inválida

@enduml